This project is a fork and combines code from two upstream projects. The full
attribution and license notices for each are below.

1. Home Assistant Core — EZVIZ integration
------------------------------------------
Source: https://github.com/home-assistant/core/tree/dev/homeassistant/components/ezviz
License: Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE)
Copyright the Home Assistant authors.

The whole integration is derived from it; every platform file (alarm panel,
binary sensor, button, camera, config flow, const, coordinator, entity, image,
light, number, select, sensor, siren, switch, update, strings, icons) is taken
from there, with the cloud live-stream additions described in the README.

Original EZVIZ integration author / codeowner: RenierM26 (@RenierM26).

2. ezviz-cloud-hass
-------------------
Source: https://github.com/bvis/ezviz-cloud-hass
License: MIT
Copyright (c) 2026 Basilio Vera (@bvis).

The cloud (VTM) live-view code in this fork (custom_components/ezviz_rtsp/
cloud_stream.py and live.py, and the cloud branches of camera.py and
config_flow.py) is adapted from it.

3. hls.js (bundled)
-------------------
Source: https://github.com/video-dev/hls.js
License: Apache License 2.0
Copyright (c) 2017 Dailymotion (http://www.dailymotion.com)

The file custom_components/ezviz_rtsp/frontend/hls.min.js is the unmodified
hls.js v1.5.20 build, bundled so the Lovelace card never loads code from a public
CDN. Its license text is kept next to it in frontend/hls.min.js.LICENSE.txt.

